// boxcxx — <stacktrace>  ([stacktrace], P0881R7)
//
// A stacktrace is two capabilities wearing one name: walking the stack, and
// naming what you find there. BoxOS had the first from the day the DWARF
// unwinder shipped (_Unwind_Backtrace, Ф4) and did not have the second at all
// — the loader maps PT_LOAD, so an image's .symtab is not in its own address
// space, and no amount of C++ could conjure a name out of an address.
//
// Ф37 built the missing half as an OS capability rather than a library trick:
// Nameplate, a table generated at link time from the image's own symbols and
// linked in as an allocatable section. box/nameplate.h is its face; this
// header is the standard's face on top of it. That is why a lookup here costs
// a binary search and touches nothing else — no syscall, no allocation, no
// lock — which matters, because a stacktrace is usually taken while something
// is already going wrong.
//
// ── What this implementation does not have, and why ────────────────────────
//
//   source_file() is always "" and source_line() always 0. The standard
//   allows exactly this ([stacktrace.entry.obs] returns an empty string /
//   zero when the information is unavailable), and the reason is measured
//   rather than chosen: line numbers live in .debug_line, and the C++ images
//   — the only ones that can call this header — must ship without .debug_*
//   to fit the 16 MB TagFS image at all (with -g, cxxtest.elf grows about
//   tenfold). An honest zero everywhere beats line numbers in the images
//   that do not need them and silence in the ones that do.
//
//   description() returns the MANGLED name. There is no demangler in the
//   tree, and doing it at build time was measured and rejected: demangling
//   cxxtest's names grows them from 3.67 MB to 9.71 MB, single names reaching
//   5266 characters. A demangler is its own piece of work and would serve
//   more than this header.
//
//   A trace stops where the CFI stops. C sources build with
//   -fno-asynchronous-unwind-tables, so a chain that reaches boxlib or _start
//   ends there — the same boundary the exception unwinder already has.
#ifndef BOXCXX_STACKTRACE
#define BOXCXX_STACKTRACE

// [version.syn] names this header as the owner of the macro below.
#define BOXCXX_OWNS_stacktrace
#include <__bits/version_stacktrace>

#include <compare>
#include <cstddef>
#include <cstdint>
#include <format>
#include <iterator>
#include <memory>
#include <memory_resource>
#include <ostream>
